WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.554
Dive profile tabs, part one: reading the Pressure tab.

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:11.534
Same dive as before. Click Pressure, then go full screen.

00:00:11.684 --> 00:00:19.440
The orange dashed line is ambient pressure, the total pressure around you. Read it on the right-hand axis, in bar.

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:26.951
At the surface it is 1 bar, the atmosphere. Every 10 m of water adds another bar.

00:00:27.101 --> 00:00:33.306
So at 40 m you are under 5 bar, and the line stays flat while you stay on the bottom.

00:00:33.456 --> 00:00:42.011
The pressure line is the depth profile turned upside down: deeper on the left axis, higher pressure on the right.

00:00:42.161 --> 00:00:52.142
On the way up, each stop, 3 m shallower, is 0.3 bar less. Between 10 m and the surface, the pressure halves, from 2 bar to 1.

00:00:52.292 --> 00:00:58.820
That is the biggest relative change of the ascent: a volume of gas doubles there.

00:00:58.970 --> 00:01:05.475
After surfacing, the line stays at 1 bar for the rest of the chart, the start of the surface interval.

00:01:05.625 --> 00:01:17.081
The sandbox follows the EN 13319 standard, 1 bar per 10 m. Under Environment you can pick fresh or sea water, or an altitude.

00:01:17.231 --> 00:01:20.891
Next: partial pressures. Thanks for watching!
